From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=A1nos=20Mik=C3=B3?=
 <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 17:53:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 017/154] atrium: give Atrium windows an extension keybinding
 registry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

InitPostWindowConstruction resolved views::FocusManager exactly two ways -
BrowserView::GetBrowserViewForBrowser, else WebUIBrowserWindow::FromBrowser.
AtriumBrowserWindow is neither, despite owning a real views::Widget, so
focus_manager stayed null on every chromeless window, the "can be null in
tests" gate skipped ExtensionKeybindingRegistryViews, and nothing was left for
accelerator dispatch to find - a default-bound MV3 command registered and
showed in chrome://extensions/shortcuts but never fired commands.onCommand,
while Cmd+T worked on the identical input path.

Add a third branch reaching the live widget the same way the existing block at
the tail of this function does, gated identically on
IsAtriumBrowserWindowEnabled() && is_type_normal() so only windows that
actually get an AtriumBrowserWindow are affected. The downstream half already
worked: AtriumCommandDispatcherDelegate falls through to super's
prePerformKeyEquivalent, which calls eventHandledByViewsFocusManager. Teardown
at extension_keybinding_registry_.reset() was already unconditional.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../internal/browser_window_features.cc             | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_window/internal/browser_window_features.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_window/internal/browser_window_features.cc
index 0ab887d1ada99..d12b1e32471cd 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_window/internal/browser_window_features.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_window/internal/browser_window_features.cc
@@ -650,6 +650,19 @@ void BrowserWindowFeatures::InitPostWindowConstruction(Browser* browser) {
     focus_manager = browser_view->GetFocusManager();
   } else if (webui_browser_window) {
     focus_manager = webui_browser_window->widget()->GetFocusManager();
+  } else if (atrium::IsAtriumBrowserWindowEnabled() &&
+             browser->is_type_normal()) {
+    // Atrium: AtriumBrowserWindow is neither a BrowserView nor a
+    // WebUIBrowserWindow, so both lookups above miss and focus_manager would
+    // stay null -- which silently skips ExtensionKeybindingRegistryViews and
+    // leaves the extensions commands API dead on chromeless windows. Reach the
+    // real widget the same way the block at the end of this function
+    // does, and gate identically (browser_window_factory.cc) so this only
+    // fires for windows that actually get an AtriumBrowserWindow.
+    if (views::Widget* const widget = views::Widget::GetWidgetForNativeWindow(
+            browser->window()->GetNativeWindow())) {
+      focus_manager = widget->GetFocusManager();
+    }
   }
 
   // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
